Package: OmicSelector
Type: Package
Title: Biomarker Signature Selection from High-Throughput Omics Experiments
Version: 2.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Konrad", "Stawiski", , "konrad.stawiski@umed.lodz.pl", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6550-3384")),
    person("Marcin", "Kaszkowiak", role = "aut"),
    person("Damian", "Mikulski", role = "ctb"))
Description: OmicSelector is a comprehensive environment and R package for biomarker 
    signature selection from high-throughput omics experiments. Originally developed for 
    miRNA-seq, but applicable to RNA-seq, proteomics, and other multi-dimensional datasets.
    The package provides automatic and structured feature selection using 70+ methods,
    followed by benchmarking with multiple machine learning approaches to identify the
    most robust signatures for biomarker validation studies. Includes deep learning
    capabilities with Keras/TensorFlow integration, modern tidymodels workflows, and 
    comprehensive visualization tools. Features include parallel processing, automated 
    hyperparameter tuning, and extensive diagnostic plots.
